  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mr.Sakthivel vs / on 4 December, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.427 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 04.12.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.4271 of 2019 and W.M.P.(MD)Nos.3386 & 3387 of 2019 Mr.Sakthivel ... Petitioner /Vs./ 1. The Commissioner, Tamilnadu Food Safety and Drugs Administration, 359, Anna Salai, Chennai-6. 2. The Designated Officer, Tamilnadu Food Safety and Drugs Administration (Food Safety Wing), D.D.H.S. Office, Old District Board Office Compound, Salem-636 001. 3. The Food Safety Officer, Tamilnadu Food Safety and Drugs Administration (Food Safety Wing), Arcot Union, Salem District 4. The District Revenue Officer/ Adjudication Officer, Salem, Salem District. .. Respondents Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of Ind issue a writ of Certiorari, call for the records pursuant to the im 1/8 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(Md order passed by the 4th respondent vide proceedings in Na.ka.No. 21268/17/17 dated 24.08.2018 and quash the same as illegal and agai Mr.Sakthivel vs / on 4 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/109533351/ 1 the Section and Procedure under the Food Safety and Standards Act 2 Rules 2011. For Petitioner : Mr.S.Sarvagan Prabhu For Respondents : Mr.S.Shanmugavel Additional Government Pleader Order",
    "facts": "It was sent tot he Food Analysis test. The food analysis https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis report dated 24.03.2017, opined that the sample is mis-branded under Section 3(1)(zf) (c) (I) of the Food Safety and Standards Act (hereinafter referred as the Act). On receipt of the said report, the third respondent filed a charge sheet for adjudication by the fourth respondent. The petitioner was served with notice dated 06.11.2017, thereby directed the petitioner to appear before the fourth respondent for adjudication on 17.11.2017. However, without furnishing any copy of the complaint and the other document, the fourth respondent/ adjudicating authority passed the order dated 24.08.2018, thereby, imposed a fine of Rs.1,00,000/- payable by the petitioner. It should annexed the analysis report as contemplated under the Rules. However, the petitioner was not provided with any of the documents and mechanically passed the order as if the petitioner to appear before the fourth respondent on 24.08.2018, admitted their guilt. Accordingly, the designatory officer must sent one copy of the food safety operator for sample lifted. Admittedly, the petitioner being the manufacturer of Kumaran Sambar Power is not entitled for any documents. That apart, on perusal of the entire records revealed that the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis petitioner had appeared before the fourth respondent on 24.08.2018 and made a statement stating that it was happened on first time and hereafter, it will not be happened and sought for apology and also undertaken not to sell such mis-branded food products. On recording their statement, the fourth respondent imposed a fine of Rs.1,00,000/- against the petitioner, who is being the manufacturer.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
